+# Released TMU line1078 transcript memorandum: source labels and completeness questions
+
+October30,2026. Existing B129 /PD01–PD04 /FAA01–FAA04 and REC03 source-coverage queue. **A newly acquired two-page FAA memorandum names TMU commercial line1078 and a1255–1316UTC range, matching the printed transcript range of one earlier Item16candidate.** It is not the Operations Manager transcript initially sought. Its connection to the exact Item16enclosure/copy remains unverified; the one-minute transcript/rerecording label difference remains unresolved.
+
+## Original acquired and completely image-read
+
+NARA [7599161 /AWA937](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7599161) exposes the [two-page PDF](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/5-Miscellaneous/c-Transcripts/5-AWA-937-Memorandum-Fill-Transcript-New-York-ARTCC.pdf). Acquired2026-10-30T16:40:07–08UTC, HTTP200,application/pdf, **27,138bytes**, SHA256 **a10386e4e39d455c7438328eca88bb28a76b7aea5c33282b4537779924851432**. Both page images were read. The original remains unchanged in the verified source store; raw scan, signature/name/contact material and full extraction are excluded from this derivative. A released PDF and its hash identify the retrieved entity; they do not authenticate native authoring, signing, transmission, the original tape or complete production.
+
+## Preserve the source observations side by side
+
+| Source layer / locator | Observation | What remains unknown |
+|---|---|---|
+| Catalog and URL filename | **Fill Transcript** | Whether this label is a caption or cataloguing difference; it does not determine the original's status. |
+| Physical1subject; text lines8–10 | **Full Transcript; AAL11** | Meaning and scope of Full in this particular product; no native-version or assembly authentication. |
+| Physical1date; line13 | **January17,2002** | This is the printed memorandum date, not independently proven file creation, transmission or certification time. |
+| Physical1addressee; line12 | **Aircraft Accident File ZBW-ARTCC-148** | Exact case/enclosure/version crosswalk. A file label does not independently identify every conversation's aircraft. |
+| Physical1range; lines16–18 | **TMUcommercial line1078; September11,2001,1255–1316UTC** | Actual recording/channel/copy correspondence, source clock or final audible timestamp. |
+| Physical1body; lines36–42 | Six minute markers1255through1300 and **one visible time-stamped utterance at1300:41** | Whether the underlying record contains more material; what unrepresented intervals contain. Speech text and speaker-identifying fields are not republished. |
+| Physical2work-file reference; line3 | **UAL175_R42_memo.doc** | Whether the work-file reference identifies the actual native source, a reused filename/template or another assembly/version. |
+| Physical2footer; line4 | Footer date token **09/27/2001** | Its purpose and relationship to the printed January2002date; other personal/contact portions of the footer are excluded. |
+| Physical1layout; lines1–7 | Visible pagination/masthead placeholder | Document-preparation and version context; placeholder text is not proof the substantive content is false. |
+
+The subject's **AAL11**, accident-file reference and work-file name's **UAL175/R42** remain as different source fields. No flight label is selected as correct, no source is silently repaired, and no concealed/redacted identity is reconstructed. A conversation can concern more than one aircraft; a filename can be reused; incomplete conversion/assembly is another possibility. These are untested alternatives, not adopted explanations. The visible utterance alone does not identify its aircraft referent.
+
+Physical2contains a routing/footer block and no further visible time-coded dialogue. This supports a statement about the **acquired two-page entity**, not a conclusion that the underlying audio or Word file was cut. The certification itself is qualified to conversations pertaining to the subject aircraft accident. Consequently, a declared time span and a sparse related-event transcription do not by themselves establish missing speech. Native versions, complete page/attachment manifests and matched source media are the discriminating inputs.
+
+## Compare with the previously acquired inventory without resolving it
+
+The [Item16study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/62a102da31cc82a7216dc41e60bed185a11c8d45/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-response-labels-2026-10-30/README.md), physical15/printed8and16/printed9ofits original, records NewYorkTMU **1255–1315UTC rerecording** and **1255–1316UTC full transcript**. The new memorandum's facility/role/start/end provide a closer **candidate counterpart**, now with a line identifier. They do not prove it is the exact listed or delivered copy, or that any audio ends at1315. The earlier four/two/one/zero-minute label calculations remain unchanged. No recording was acquired, decoded, listened to, aligned, trimmed or repaired in this step, and no duration of missing audio is inferred.
+
+The NewYorkOperationsManager **1230–1344UTC** original and the matching rerecording/certification chain remain TODOs. Metadata-only NOM1230–1430audio candidates were located but not equated to OperationsManager or to this TMUline. Other catalog titles refer to ATCSCCNOMpositions; an acronym alone supplies no source/channel identity.
+
+## Keep the PDF's date layers separate
+
+Selected embedded metadata reports Creator **Canon DR-9080C TWAIN** and Producer **Adobe Acrobat10.1.8 Paper Capture Plug-in**. Its CreationDate is **D:20051222232254-05'00'** and ModDate **D:20131106161605-05'00'**. The acquired HTTP Last-Modified header is **Sat,04Sep2021 04:01:33GMT**. All are preserved by field name in [OBSERVATIONS.json](OBSERVATIONS.json) /[SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json). They are not substituted for the2001footer, January2002memorandum date or September2001recording time. These different layer/event fields do not by themselves establish an inconsistent historical clock, deliberate alteration or actual scanner/software use. Their provenance and relation remain unverified.
+
+## Reading, checks and next originals
+
+The complete51-title Miscellaneous transcript table was inspected across its six pages; individual contents were not. Two series queries were performed: the role/end compound returned no hits despite known visible matching content in the held inventory; a1230query returned433hits with only two ten-title views inspected. This is a query/index-scope limitation, not evidence that the source never existed. The initial three-description cap was explicitly extended on newly exposed concrete AWA937/AWA940locators; source/PDF-size/reading limits remained unchanged. [Actual scope](READING-SCOPE.json).
+
+The reproducer checks the exact27,138bytes/two-page source, selected visible text fields, sole time-stamped entry and filtered PDF metadata. It does not authenticate a native document, validate time or prove completeness. Both images were actually inspected separately from those machine checks. [Verifier](verify_original.py), [results](VERIFICATION.json). The entire native Word reference, original certified transcript/version, source tape/channel identifiers, preparation/review and transfer/enclosure/receipt records remain missing. [Exact targets](OPEN-RECORDS.md).
+
+The FAA correctedMay2003answer/delivery, signed consideration/action/no-action and distinct recommendation implementation/closure remain open. So do telephone carrier/native-call joins, recorder configuration/custody/independent clocks, materials authenticated-specimen/calibration joins, and steel native preservation/inventory/attribution/review-delivery inputs. Allfive tracks/eighteen substantive criteria remain unfinished. Earlier records/conflicting values remain unchanged. This public derivative contains notes/selected safe fields/code, not raw scans/DOM/fullOCR, speech, personnel/contact/signature data, private case/correspondence or strategy. [Checklist](CHECKLIST.md), [exact additions](REVISION.diff), [manifest](MANIFEST.json). Publication is verified separately from creation or commitment.
